[{:db/id -1, :adr/authoritative_for ["first real instantiation of the skill-*/action-* repository-role taxonomy (kotoba-lang/loop-ux-kaizen resources/repository-rules.edn) anywhere in kotoba-lang" "creation of kotoba-lang/skill-loop-system-dynamics and kotoba-lang/action-loop-system-dynamics"], :adr/topic "skill-action-loop-system-dynamics-scaffold", :adr/related ["kotoba-lang/loop-system-dynamics" "kotoba-lang/loop-ux-kaizen"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607220100-skill-action-loop-system-dynamics-scaffold", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-22", :adr/body "# ADR-2607220100: scaffold kotoba-lang/skill-loop-system-dynamics + kotoba-lang/action-loop-system-dynamics\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-22\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization -- new-project-scaffold flow)\n**Related**: `kotoba-lang/loop-system-dynamics` (the loop these two repos adapt), `kotoba-lang/loop-ux-kaizen` (owns the `resources/repository-rules.edn` taxonomy both repos must satisfy)\n\n## Context\n\n`loop-system-dynamics`'s own README has carried this as a documented-but-not-built \"Next\" item since its first cycle: \"A `skill-loop-system-dynamics` (agent-instruction package) and/or `action-loop-system-dynamics` (GitHub Action adapter) per the same taxonomy, once a resident CI schedule is wanted.\"\n\nBefore scaffolding, both taxonomy roles were checked against `loop-ux-kaizen`'s own `resources/repository-rules.edn` (the schema this whole `loop-*`/`skill-*`/`action-*` naming convention is defined by) and against the rest of the `kotoba-lang` org (`gh api orgs/kotoba-lang/repos --paginate .name`, 2026-07-22): **no `skill-*` or `action-*` prefixed repo exists anywhere in the org yet** -- not even the taxonomy doc's own named examples (`skill-ux-kaizen`, `action-ux-kaizen`) exist. This is therefore the first real instantiation of either role, not a copy of an existing pattern.\n\n## Decision\n\nScaffold both repos now, real and functional (not placeholder stubs), directly against the taxonomy's own `:must`/`:must-not` requirements since no other example exists to model from:\n\n### `kotoba-lang/skill-loop-system-dynamics` (role `:agent-instruction-package`)\n\n- `:must [:define-agent-procedure :declare-inputs :declare-outputs]` -- a `SKILL.md` (Claude Code's own skill format, since that's the concrete agent-instruction-package shape already in wide use across this workspace's own `.claude/skills/`) that states the real observe->evaluate->decide->act->record-evidence procedure, the real classpath/sibling-checkout inputs each `bin/run_*.cljs` needs, and the real outputs (`target/*-report.md`, `ledger/*-ledger.edn` append) -- pointing at the real commands in `loop-system-dynamics`'s own README rather than re-describing them.\n- `:must-not [:require-resident-runner :own-ci-state]` -- satisfied structurally: a skill is agent-invoked instructions read on demand, never a running process, and it does not track its own pass/fail history (that is `action-loop-system-dynamics`'s job, not this repo's).\n\n### `kotoba-lang/action-loop-system-dynamics` (role `:github-action-adapter`)\n\n- `:must [:expose-action-yml :pin-external-revisions :emit-check-result]` -- a real composite `action.yml` at repo root that checks out `loop-system-dynamics` + its real sibling deps at **pinned commit SHAs** (never floating branch/tag refs) and runs the real `nbb bin/run.cljs` cycle, failing the check (`exit 1`) if `run-cycle!` throws (the same `when-not valid?` failure path `fleet_registration_xmile.cljs`'s own `run-cycle!` already uses) -- a real CI signal, not a placeholder green check.\n- `:must-not [:own-domain-contract :hide-provider-neutral-core]` -- satisfied structurally: `action.yml` only invokes `loop-system-dynamics`'s own already-published `bin/` entry points, never reimplements observe/evaluate/decide/act itself, and `loop-system-dynamics` stays runnable identically outside GitHub Actions (nothing about its own core becomes GitHub-Actions-only).\n\nBoth repos are scaffolded via the same standing-authorized flow as every other new project in this workspace (ADR -> child-repo scaffold -> `gh repo create` (public, matching `kotoba-lang`'s own org-default visibility, `manifest/repos.edn :orgs`) -> push -> `manifest/repos.edn` `:extra-projects` registration via `gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry`).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `loop-system-dynamics`'s README \"Next\" item for this is closed; both roles now have a real, working first instance other `loop-*` repos in this workspace can copy instead of inventing their own `skill-*`/`action-*` shape from scratch.\n- Neither repo owns any scoring/domain truth of its own (per `repository-rules.edn`'s `:composition {:authority \"loop-*\" :adapters [\"action-*\" \"skill-*\"]}`) -- both are thin, and stay thin on purpose; `loop-system-dynamics` remains the sole place backlog/rate/leverage logic lives.\n- `action-loop-system-dynamics`'s CI schedule is opt-in (a workflow in a CONSUMING repo enables it by referencing this action) -- creating this repo does not itself turn on any resident schedule anywhere.\n"}]
